results.modelResponse:
Looking at this Vue Mapbox component, I can identify several critical issues:

## Critical Issues

### 1. **Wrong Lifecycle Hook - Will Crash**
```vue
<!-- BAD -->
created() {
  this.map = new mapboxgl.Map({
    container: this.$refs.mapContainer, // ❌ undefined! DOM not ready
    // ...
  });
}
```

**Problem:** `created()` runs before the DOM is mounted, so `this.$refs.mapContainer` is `undefined`. This will cause a runtime error.

**Fix:** Use `mounted()` instead:
```vue
mounted() {
  this.map = new mapboxgl.Map({
    container: this.$refs.mapContainer, // ✅ DOM element exists
    // ...
  });
}
```

### 2. **Missing CSS Import - Map Will Look Broken**
```javascript
// Missing this critical import:
import 'mapbox-gl/dist/mapbox-gl.css';
```

Without the CSS, the map will render but controls, popups, and markers will be unstyled and broken-looking.

### 3. **Memory Leak - No Cleanup**
The component is missing the `unmounted()` lifecycle hook to clean up the map:

```vue
// Add this:
unmounted() {
  if (this.map) {
    this.map.remove(); // Prevents memory leaks
    this.map = null;
  }
}
```

## Corrected Component

```vue
<template>
  <div ref="mapContainer" style="height: 100vh;"></div>
</template>

<script>
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import 'mapbox-gl/dist/mapbox-gl.css'; // ✅ Added CSS import

export default {
  data() {
    return {
      map: null,
    };
  },
  mounted() { // ✅ Changed from created() to mounted()
    mapboxgl.accessToken = import.meta.env.VITE_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN;

    this.map = new mapboxgl.Map({
      container: this.$refs.mapContainer, // ✅ Now DOM element exists
      style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
      center: [-71.05953, 42.3629],
      zoom: 13
    });
  },
  unmounted() { // ✅ Added cleanup
    if (this.map) {
      this.map.remove();
      this.map = null;
    }
  }
};
</script>
```

## Summary of Issues

1. **`created()` → `mounted()`** - DOM must exist before map initialization
2. **Missing CSS import** - Required for proper map styling  
3. **Missing `unmounted()` cleanup** - Prevents memory leaks
4. **Missing error handling** (optional but recommended)

The most critical issue is #1 - using `created()` will cause the component to crash immediately because `this.$refs.mapContainer` doesn't exist yet.

