You need the **Data Visualization Base Map pattern** for your election choropleth. This pattern is specifically designed for overlaying statistical data while providing minimal but essential geographic context.

Here's the recommended configuration for your US county election map:

## Base Map Configuration

```json
{
  "version": 8,
  "sources": {
    "mapbox-streets": {
      "type": "vector",
      "url": "mapbox://mapbox.mapbox-streets-v8"
    },
    "county-data": {
      "type": "geojson",
      "data": "your-county-election-data.geojson"
    }
  },
  "layers": [
    {
      "id": "background",
      "type": "background",
      "paint": {
        "background-color": "#f8f9fa"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "state-fills",
      "type": "fill",
      "source": "mapbox-streets",
      "source-layer": "admin",
      "filter": ["==", "admin_level", 1],
      "paint": {
        "fill-color": "#ffffff",
        "fill-opacity": 0.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "county-choropleth",
      "type": "fill",
      "source": "county-data",
      "paint": {
        "fill-color": [
          "interpolate",
          ["linear"],
          ["get", "vote_margin"],
          -50, "#b71c1c",  // Strong Republican (dark red)
          -20, "#e57373",  // Moderate Republican (light red)
          -5,  "#f8bbd9",  // Lean Republican (pink)
          0,   "#e1bee7",  // Tie (light purple)
          5,   "#c5cae9",  // Lean Democrat (light blue)
          20,  "#7986cb",  // Moderate Democrat (blue)
          50,  "#1976d2"   // Strong Democrat (dark blue)
        ],
        "fill-opacity": 0.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "county-borders",
      "type": "line",
      "source": "county-data",
      "paint": {
        "line-color": "#ffffff",
        "line-width": 0.5,
        "line-opacity": 0.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "state-borders",
      "type": "line",
      "source": "mapbox-streets",
      "source-layer": "admin",
      "filter": ["==", "admin_level", 1],
      "paint": {
        "line-color": "#424242",
        "line-width": {
          "base": 1,
          "stops": [
            [4, 1],
            [8, 2],
            [12, 3]
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "major-cities",
      "type": "symbol",
      "source": "mapbox-streets",
      "source-layer": "place_label",
      "filter": [
        "all",
        ["==", "type", "city"],
        [">", ["get", "population"], 500000]
      ],
      "layout": {
        "text-field": ["get", "name"],
        "text-size": {
          "base": 1,
          "stops": [
            [4, 10],
            [8, 14],
            [12, 16]
          ]
        },
        "text-font": ["Open Sans Semibold", "Arial Unicode MS Bold"]
      },
      "paint": {
        "text-color": "#424242",
        "text-halo-color": "#ffffff",
        "text-halo-width": 2
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Key Design Decisions

**Color Palette:** Uses a diverging red-to-blue scale that's:
- Colorblind-friendly
- Follows political convention (red=R, blue=D)
- Has neutral purple for competitive counties
- High contrast for readability

**Borders Strategy:**
- Thin white county borders (0.5px) for subtle separation
- Thicker dark state borders (1-3px) for major geographic context
- No international borders (keeps focus on US data)

**Minimal Base Elements:**
- Very light gray background (#f8f9fa)
- White state fills for subtle context
- Major cities only (500k+ population) for orientation
- No roads, parks, or other distracting features

## Data Structure Expected

Your county GeoJSON should include these properties:

```json
{
  "type": "Feature",
  "geometry": {...},
  "properties": {
    "fips": "06001",
    "county_name": "Alameda County",
    "state": "CA",
    "vote_margin": 45.2,  // Positive = Democrat margin, Negative = Republican margin
    "total_votes": 627421,
    "dem_votes": 456789,
    "rep_votes": 170632
  }
}
```

## Interactive Enhancements

Add these event handlers for better UX:

```javascript
// Hover effects
map.on('mouseenter', 'county-choropleth', (e) => {
  map.getCanvas().style.cursor = 'pointer';

  // Optional: Add hover state
  map.setPaintProperty('county-choropleth', 'fill-opacity', [
    'case',
    ['==', ['get', 'fips'], e.features[0].properties.fips],
    1.0,
    0.8
  ]);
});

map.on('mouseleave', 'county-choropleth', () => {
  map.getCanvas().style.cursor = '';
  map.setPaintProperty('county-choropleth', 'fill-opacity', 0.8);
});

// Click for details
map.on('click', 'county-choropleth', (e) => {
  const props = e.features[0].properties;
  new mapboxgl.Popup()
    .setLngLat(e.lngLat)
    .setHTML(`
      <strong>${props.county_name}, ${props.state}</strong><br>
      Margin: ${props.vote_margin > 0 ? 'D' : 'R'}+${Math.abs(props.vote_margin).toFixed(1)}%<br>
      Total votes: ${props.total_votes.toLocaleString()}
    `)
    .addTo(map);
});
```

This pattern ensures your election data is the clear focus while providing just enough geographic context for users to orient themselves and understand the results.

You need to switch to the Mapbox version of the geocoder plugin. Here's how to fix it:

## 1. Update the Package

```bash
# Remove MapLibre geocoder
npm uninstall @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder

# Install Mapbox geocoder
npm install @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder
```

## 2. Update Your Import and CSS

```javascript
// Before (MapLibre)
import MaplibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';

// After (Mapbox)
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';
```

## 3. Update Geocoder Configuration

The main difference is that the Mapbox geocoder requires your access token and a reference to the mapboxgl object:

```javascript
// Before (MapLibre) - Basic setup
const geocoder = new MaplibreGeocoder({
  maplibregl: maplibregl,
  // other options...
});

// After (Mapbox) - Add token and mapboxgl reference
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken, // Required!
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl, // Required!
  // other options work the same...
});

map.addControl(geocoder);
```

## 4. Complete Working Example

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import 'mapbox-gl/dist/mapbox-gl.css';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

// Set your token
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.your_mapbox_access_token';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.4194, 37.7749],
  zoom: 12
});

// Add geocoder with proper configuration
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken, // ← Required
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl, // ← Required
  placeholder: 'Search for places',
  proximity: {
    longitude: -122.4194,
    latitude: 37.7749
  }
});

map.addControl(geocoder);
```

## 5. All Other Options Stay the Same

The good news is that all other geocoder options work identically:

```javascript
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,

  // All these options work exactly the same as MapLibre version
  placeholder: 'Search for places',
  bbox: [-122.5, 37.7, -122.3, 37.8],
  proximity: { longitude: -122.4194, latitude: 37.7749 },
  countries: 'us,ca',
  types: 'place,locality,neighborhood',
  limit: 10,
  language: 'en',
  flyTo: {
    bearing: 0,
    speed: 2,
    curve: 1,
    easing: function(t) { return t; }
  }
});

// Events work the same
geocoder.on('result', (e) => {
  console.log('Selected:', e.result);
});

geocoder.on('error', (e) => {
  console.error('Geocoder error:', e.error);
});
```

## 6. Benefits of Mapbox Geocoder

After switching, you get access to Mapbox's premium geocoding:

- **Better Results**: More accurate and comprehensive place data
- **Global Coverage**: Worldwide address and place search
- **Auto-complete**: Real-time suggestions as you type
- **Multiple Languages**: Support for local language results
- **Rich Metadata**: Detailed place information and context

## CDN Alternative

If you prefer CDN over npm:

```html
<!-- Add after mapbox-gl.js -->
<script src='https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v5.0.0/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js'></script>
<link rel='stylesheet' href='https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v5.0.0/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css' type='text/css' />

<script>
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl
});
map.addControl(geocoder);
</script>
```

## Quick Checklist

- [ ] Uninstall `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`
- [ ] Install `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`
- [ ] Update import statement
- [ ] Update CSS import
- [ ] Add `accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken` to geocoder config
- [ ] Add `mapboxgl: mapboxgl` to geocoder config
- [ ] Test search functionality

That's it! The geocoder will now work with your Mapbox GL JS setup and provide enhanced search capabilities.

You're creating a performance bottleneck by creating new `PointAnnotationManager` instances repeatedly. Here's how to fix it:

## Problem
Creating new annotation managers on every refresh is expensive and causes memory leaks.

## Solution: Reuse the Manager

**Create the manager once and reuse it:**

```kotlin
class MapActivity : AppCompatActivity() {
    private lateinit var mapView: MapView
    private lateinit var pointAnnotationManager: PointAnnotationManager // Store as class property

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_map)

        mapView = findViewById(R.id.mapView)
        mapView.mapboxMap.loadStyle(Style.STANDARD)

        // Create manager ONCE
        pointAnnotationManager = mapView.annotations.createPointAnnotationManager()
    }

    // Optimized refresh method
    fun refreshMarkers(locations: List<MarkerData>) {
        // Clear existing markers
        pointAnnotationManager.deleteAll()

        // Create new annotations
        val annotations = locations.map { location ->
            PointAnnotationOptions()
                .withPoint(Point.fromLngLat(location.lng, location.lat))
                .withIconImage("marker")
        }

        // Batch create all at once (much faster than individual creates)
        pointAnnotationManager.create(annotations)
    }
}
```

**For Jetpack Compose:**

```kotlin
@Composable
fun MapScreen(locations: List<MarkerData>) {
    var pointAnnotationManager by remember { mutableStateOf<PointAnnotationManager?>(null) }

    MapboxMap(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {
        // Create manager once
        MapEffect(Unit) { mapView ->
            mapView.mapboxMap.loadStyle(Style.STANDARD)
            pointAnnotationManager = mapView.annotations.createPointAnnotationManager()
        }

        // Update markers when data changes
        MapEffect(locations) { mapView ->
            pointAnnotationManager?.let { manager ->
                manager.deleteAll()

                val annotations = locations.map { location ->
                    PointAnnotationOptions()
                        .withPoint(Point.fromLngLat(location.lng, location.lat))
                        .withIconImage("marker")
                }

                manager.create(annotations)
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Additional Performance Tips

**1. Limit visible markers to viewport:**
```kotlin
fun refreshMarkers(locations: List<MarkerData>) {
    val visibleBounds = mapView.mapboxMap.coordinateBoundsForCamera(
        mapView.mapboxMap.cameraState.toCameraOptions()
    )

    val visibleLocations = locations.filter { location ->
        visibleBounds.contains(Point.fromLngLat(location.lng, location.lat))
    }

    // Only create annotations for visible markers
    updateAnnotations(visibleLocations)
}
```

**2. Use clustering for many markers:**
```kotlin
// For 100+ markers, consider using clustering
val clusterOptions = ClusterOptions.Builder()
    .clusterRadius(50)
    .clusterMaxZoom(14)
    .build()

pointAnnotationManager = mapView.annotations.createPointAnnotationManager(clusterOptions)
```

## Key Changes Summary

- ✅ **Create manager once** - Store as class property
- ✅ **Reuse manager** - Call `deleteAll()` then `create()`  
- ✅ **Batch operations** - Create all annotations at once
- ✅ **Consider clustering** - For many markers
- ✅ **Viewport culling** - Only show visible markers

This should dramatically improve your performance by eliminating the repeated manager creation overhead.

For 50MB of point data (millions of GPS records), you need a completely different approach than GeoJSON. Here are the best strategies:

## 1. Vector Tiles (Recommended)

Convert your data to vector tiles for optimal performance:

```bash
# Install tippecanoe (vector tile generator)
# macOS: brew install tippecanoe
# Ubuntu: apt-get install tippecanoe

# Convert GeoJSON to vector tiles
tippecanoe -o gps-data.mbtiles \
  --maximum-zoom=14 \
  --minimum-zoom=0 \
  --drop-densest-as-needed \
  --extend-zooms-if-still-dropping \
  your-gps-data.geojson
```

Then serve the tiles and use them:

```javascript
map.on('load', () => {
  map.addSource('gps-points', {
    type: 'vector',
    tiles: ['https://your-server.com/tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf'],
    minzoom: 0,
    maxzoom: 14
  });

  // Show as heatmap at low zoom
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'gps-heatmap',
    type: 'heatmap',
    source: 'gps-points',
    'source-layer': 'your-layer-name', // From tippecanoe output
    maxzoom: 9,
    paint: {
      'heatmap-weight': 1,
      'heatmap-intensity': ['interpolate', ['linear'], ['zoom'], 0, 1, 9, 3],
      'heatmap-color': [
        'interpolate',
        ['linear'],
        ['heatmap-density'],
        0, 'rgba(33,102,172,0)',
        0.2, 'rgb(103,169,207)',
        0.4, 'rgb(209,229,240)', 
        0.6, 'rgb(253,219,199)',
        0.8, 'rgb(239,138,98)',
        1, 'rgb(178,24,43)'
      ],
      'heatmap-radius': ['interpolate', ['linear'], ['zoom'], 0, 2, 9, 20]
    }
  });

  // Show individual points at high zoom
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'gps-points',
    type: 'circle',
    source: 'gps-points',
    'source-layer': 'your-layer-name',
    minzoom: 9,
    paint: {
      'circle-radius': ['interpolate', ['linear'], ['zoom'], 9, 1, 16, 4],
      'circle-color': '#ff4444',
      'circle-opacity': 0.6
    }
