For your real-time fleet tracking scenario, you need a **hybrid architecture** that combines the Mapbox MCP Server for zone management with direct Turf.js for the hot path checks.

## Recommended Architecture

### Hot Path: Direct Turf.js (Not MCP)
For your 50 trucks × every 2 seconds = 25 containment checks per second, **don't use MCP tools for the real-time checks**. The network overhead and agent reasoning time makes it impractical.

```javascript
// In your application (not via MCP)
import { booleanPointInPolygon } from '@turf/boolean-point-in-polygon';

// Real-time check (runs 25 times/second)
function checkTruckInZones(truckCoordinate, restrictedZones) {
  for (const zone of restrictedZones) {
    const isInside = booleanPointInPolygon(
      [truckCoordinate.longitude, truckCoordinate.latitude],
      zone.geometry
    );

    if (isInside !== truck.wasInZone[zone.id]) {
      // State change detected - truck entered or left zone
      handleZoneEvent(truck, zone, isInside);
    }
  }
}
```

### Cold Path: Mapbox MCP Server
Use MCP tools for zone management, visualization, and peripheral tasks:

## Complete Implementation Strategy

### 1. Zone Definition & Management (MCP)

